<===> README.md
When a parent selector list has line breaks (`.a,` and `.b` on separate
lines) and the nested selector follows `&` with a combinator (`& ~ .c`),
the line breaks were lost in the output (they were kept for `&:hover`).
Expected output generated with dart-sass 1.93.1.
<===>
================================================================================
<===> extend/extender_line_break/input.scss
.x ~ .y {a: b}
.p,
.q {@extend .x}
<===> extend/extender_line_break/output.css
.x ~ .y, .p ~ .y,
.q ~ .y {
  a: b;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> parent/child/input.scss
.a,
.b {
  & > .c {x: y}
}
<===> parent/child/output.css
.a > .c,
.b > .c {
  x: y;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> parent/compound/input.scss
.a,
.b {
  &:hover {x: y}
}
<===> parent/compound/output.css
.a:hover,
.b:hover {
  x: y;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> parent/no_line_break/input.scss
.a, .b {
  & ~ .c {x: y}
}
<===> parent/no_line_break/output.css
.a ~ .c, .b ~ .c {
  x: y;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> parent/several/input.scss
.a,
.b {
  & + .c, & > .d {x: y}
}
<===> parent/several/output.css
.a + .c, .a > .d,
.b + .c,
.b > .d {
  x: y;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> parent/sibling/input.scss
.a,
.b {
  & ~ .c {x: y}
}
<===> parent/sibling/output.css
.a ~ .c,
.b ~ .c {
  x: y;
}
